  "critical_findings": [
    "PR118 is the integer/non-monotonic sizing owner. Its current economics contract is SOL/WSOL lamports; no USDC atom relabeling.",
    "AGG05 ConflictAwareScheduler is in-memory, uses an RLock and delegates reservations. No general read-only account set is represented in WorkResourceSet.",
    "OpportunityResourceFootprint includes writable accounts and separate oracles; the scheduler adapter currently copies pools and writes, not a full account access-mode map.",
    "The inspected DurableLifecycleStore explicitly rejects topology other than single-node. Do not share its SQLite file across machines.",
    "MPR19 and single_truth are existing authority/review surfaces. Their presence is not proof of a complete runtime cutover; map the actual application path before distributed admission.",
    "Scheduler reaping releases expired work through its reservation port. Future post-submission unknown outcomes must stay held under the lifecycle authority, not be released by this compute queue.",
    "PR356 allocation is bounded research allocation; ensure complete units/budget dimensions and do not describe sums of supplied tail scores as joint CVaR.",
    "OrderbookAmmStrategy remains disabled pending verified subscriptions."
